# Castor EDC in Livebook

```elixir
# The checkout this notebook is in, and ex_castor_edc checked out next to it
# (or where CASTOR_EDC_PATH says). Outside a checkout, use
# {:ex_castor_edc_kino, "~> 0.1.0"} instead.
castor_edc = System.get_env("CASTOR_EDC_PATH", Path.expand("../../ex_castor_edc", __DIR__))

Mix.install([
  {:ex_castor_edc_kino, path: Path.expand("..", __DIR__)},
  {:ex_castor_edc, path: castor_edc, override: true}
])
```

## Introduction

This notebook connects to Castor EDC, picks a study and looks around it, without writing any setup code.
Everything here only reads: nothing in it changes the study.

Add your API credentials as Livebook secrets first: `CASTOR_EDC_CLIENT_ID` and `CASTOR_EDC_CLIENT_SECRET` (create them on your [account settings page](https://data.castoredc.com/account/settings)).
The connection cell reads them from there, so they never appear in the notebook.

## Connecting

Pick the server your studies are on, and test the connection.

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":"","chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.CastorEDC.Kino.ConnectionCell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
client =
  CastorEDC.new(
    client_id: System.fetch_env!("LB_CASTOR_EDC_CLIENT_ID"),
    client_secret: System.fetch_env!("LB_CASTOR_EDC_CLIENT_SECRET"),
    base_url: "https://data.castoredc.com"
  )
```

## Picking a study

Once the client exists, this cell lists the studies it can reach.

